            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hi!\r\n\r\nThe answer is \"probably, yes\", but it is not really designed to do so. Depending on the use case, I'd suggest:\r\n- Adding `---@private` to any section that you don't want 'mini.doc' to touch.\r\n- Adjust [all/necessary hooks](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/5d938b3a078a7eeae23ba9f04f180066ab8bd9ef/doc/mini-doc.txt#L180-L197) to do nothing.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The answer is \"probably, yes\", but it is not really designed to do so. Depending on the use case, I'd suggest:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Adding <code class=\"notranslate\">---@private</code> to any section that you don't want 'mini.doc' to touch.</li>\n<li>Adjust <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/5d938b3a078a7eeae23ba9f04f180066ab8bd9ef/doc/mini-doc.txt#L180-L197\">all/necessary hooks</a> to do nothing.</li>\n</ul>",
            "bodyText": "Hi!\nThe answer is \"probably, yes\", but it is not really designed to do so. Depending on the use case, I'd suggest:\n\nAdding ---@private to any section that you don't want 'mini.doc' to touch.\nAdjust all/necessary hooks to do nothing.",
